    "body": "Quick pass (author side, not a review) - head 9f0c42f8, the remaining items from the 12:47Z review:\n\n1. **`wear` is sinker-only.** Before this, `parse_conditions` read `wear` on a wire machine and kept it unused. It is now refused by condition id and key, the same way `undersize` is: `edm condition \"C1\" wear is a sinker field; this is a wire_edm machine`. `Edm::fits` now counts a stated `wear` as a sinker key, so a hand-edited parsed wire machine carrying one is not `is_sane` either (`crates/post/src/machine/edm_conditions.rs`, `crates/post/src/machine/edm.rs`).\n2. **Tests.**\n   - New: `machine::edm_conditions::tests::a_wear_rate_is_a_sinker_field` (post: refused in the file, accepted on a sinker, the parsed wire machine is not sane) and `edm_conditions::a_wire_machine_stating_wear_is_refused_by_name` (app).\n   - Already covered by `sinker_wear::a_bad_wear_rate_is_refused_by_name`: the out-of-range rates (1.0, -0.1, 2) and a non-number `\"fast\"`. NaN can't be written in JSON. A NaN measured rate on the op is refused in that same test.\n3. **Decision file.** `docs/decisions/546-sinker-wear-comp.md` now says:\n   - the rate is per mm of cavity depth below the work top, not per mm of tip travel;\n   - a misstated rate over- or under-burns by (stated - true) x depth;\n   - the stock sim judges the burn at the stated rate, so it can't catch this.\n\nTest results on 9f0c42f8 (debug):\n- `cargo test -p camcraft-post --lib edm`: 20 passed.\n- app `edm_conditions` 2, `edm_machine` 5, `sinker_wear` 6, `sinker_burn` 8, all passed.\n- `cargo clippy -p camcraft-post -p camcraft-app --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\nNot run: the full quick or batch gate. Labels are left for the maintainer.\n",
